{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123022-mta-newbie-gm-question","id":1123022,"title":"MTA - Newbie GM question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-31T08:07:43-07:00","id":1123022,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> MTA - Newbie GM question","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hello all.<br /> <br /> <i>Excuse me if I don't post in the correct topic, it is my very first post.</i><br /> <br /> I have been a GM for VtM and WtA for many years (9 and 6 repectively) and never got to play/GM MtA but I have now such opportunity to GM a game I've never played.<br /> <br /> I have been asked by one of my potential players if there is an equivalent of Ghoul (VtM) or Kinfolk (WtA) in Mage. My searches thru the material I have (MtA revised and Sorcerer's Crusade) were unsuccessful so far. To be precise, what I'm looking for is a kind of &quot;improved&quot; human the same way Ghouls have a blood pool (I'm thinking limited Quintessence with maybe an Arete rating of 1) and/or could develop the first level (perception) of some spheres (same way Ghouls can use some disciplines and Kinfolks do use some gifts. If it exists, could you also be kind enough to point me to source material so I could acquire it on DriveThruRPG. If it doesn't an alternative would be users of Hedge Magic but I understand the mechanics aren't the same.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.</b> </span></span></span><br /> \u2026<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Leonardo da Vinci</i></span></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13746-matteo-the-solificato","name":"Matteo the Solificato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:55:47-07:00","id":1123034,"title":"","content":"There is no such thing in M20.<br /> You could always use hedge magic, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:07:17-07:00","id":1123039,"title":"","content":"The closest thing to a Ghoul or Kinfolk in Mage are the Acolytes - mortals that essentially are the right hands of Mages, and in the case of Sorcerors also form a large chunk of their groups in later editions - in bigger numbers than the Mages themselves as awakening to True Magick is a fickle and unplannable thing, for the most part.<br /> <br /> Sorcerors (and the other plain unawakened humans with other Numina) essentially use linear magic - that is, discipline-style ranked abilities, for the most part.<br /> Hence the hedge magic that Goran is mentioning.<br /> You can find out more about Sorcerors in the book of the same name, the latest being Sorceror Revised, and can use all the other Numina you can find in other books that refer to unawakened/normal humans with special abilities.<br /> <br /> Of course not all the unawakened rank and file of Mage groups have special abilities - far from it, many are literally plain humans that just help out in ways they can, and form the backbone. But they are in good surroundings to learn linear magic and numina, and otherwise can get benefits from their benefactors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-31-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:21:27-07:00","id":1123041,"title":"","content":"There isn't a &quot;half mage splat&quot; that serves mages (in a sense, all humans are full mages, it's just that they're asleep), you could say that all weird However, Mages can and do enhance humans. The enhancements aren't limited to a few standard rules like Ghouls, though, they can be anything reachable by rote. Technocracy likes their cyborgs and mutants, many Traditions bless their human alies making them superhuman.<br /> Giving a human lvl 1 sensory effects would be useful for any mage but, granted, the power to create these enhancements isn't as ubiquitous as the power to create ghouls it's in vampire, thus it isn't common (well, in the Technocracy isn't rare, but that speaks of the kind of resources they have). It's more likely for prized Acolites to get temporal magic efects casted at them (i.e: you can share magical perceptions with Sphere at 2) or minnor artifacts, when they get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-31-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T09:37:48-07:00","id":1123525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123022-mta-newbie-gm-question?p=1123041#post1123041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in a sense, all humans are full mages, it's just that they're asleep</div> </div> </div> </div>That part always elude me, but you're very right! That's why there is no equivalent of Ghoul/Kinfolk. My player wanted &quot;enhanced&quot; or &quot;special&quot; allies/retainers, now I know exctly how I will approach the request. Thanks a million.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.</b> </span></span></span><br /> \u2026<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Leonardo da Vinci</i></span></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13746-matteo-the-solificato","name":"Matteo the Solificato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:40:29-07:00","id":1123544,"title":"","content":"The closest analogue is probably an Extraordinary Citizen in the Technocracy. They are not awakened, but do not count as a sleeper for Technocratic procedures and can use some hypertech devices. M20 has suggested stats for them on pages 623 - 624.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:57:43-07:00","id":1123584,"title":"","content":"Actually, Acolites work like that too. Acolites do not count as a sleeper for whatever magick they believe in (they aren't witness) and can use Talismans and Charms of whatever Paradigm they believe in. This is not a &quot;special&quot; splat, but rather the fact that anyone educated into a Paradigm can use the magic items of said paradigm and won't count as a witness (Technocrats &quot;create&quot; educated Citizens with their Social Conditioning, but they can appear &quot;naturaly&quot; among people with inclination for a certain mystical or scientifical Focus)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-01-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:58:42-07:00","id":1123585,"title":"","content":"You'd call them consors from <i>Ascension's Right Hand</i>. Essentially, build them as a normal human and give them some merits which reflect supernatural abilities. You could use Numina, Psychic powers or sorcerer paths. The major advantages of consors are that they believe their mage friend's paradigm and might be able to use Devices/Wonders/Talismans/magical doohickies that those who need not be Awakened used.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if I'm doing Mage, the cool stuff is exploring being someone who can tweak reality with belief and focus. So, consors are good as NPCs or good if you want to do more Ars Magica Troupe style play and have someone who is not playing a Mage that session play a capable associate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T12:24:16-07:00","id":1124876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123022-mta-newbie-gm-question?p=1123585#post1123585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd call them consors from <i>Ascension's Right Hand</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I will look into this!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.</b> </span></span></span><br /> \u2026<br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Leonardo da Vinci</i></span></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13746-matteo-the-solificato","name":"Matteo the Solificato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}